<title>CHINA: China, Israel in potassium chloride initial pact.</title>
<headline>China, Israel in potassium chloride initial pact.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China and Israel have signed a memorandum of understanding on a joint venture to produce 800,000 tonnes of potassium chloride annually in western China, the Economic Information Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China and Israel have held six rounds of talks on the project in the western province of Qinghai since 1995, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>In the latest round, the two sides reached consensus on the joint venture contract and the use of technology, it said without giving further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
